WEBVTT

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:15.890
-God also needs it.
-…walk to Mars.

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:19.850
I don't need the future!

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.350
…Seven.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:31.610
That strange dream again.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.110
What the hell!

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.910
I forgot. We got gravity two days ago.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.880
Gravity sucks.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:57.890
My cognitive limiter… is off!

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:00.010
John Doe's tool worked great.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.140
Touya, did you unlock
your cognitive limiter again?

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.310
Don't look, Chief.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:07.900
You're going to get in trouble
with your uncle again.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.570
This one is hard to spot, so I'll be fine.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.320
Me Dakky!

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.530
Even though you unlocked the limiter,
you're still stupid.

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:19.820
Language and cognitive ability
are unrelated.

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:20.830
GRAVITY

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:24.450
Dakky, where does
your cognition level stand?

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.790
Look at that.
It's twice what it was before.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:31.460
I finally broke through the B limiter.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.460
Poopy!

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:38.130
-First-stage separation confirmed…
-All right. This is it.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.600
Launch control Japan Ex-terra 607…

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:42.600
ADAPTED

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:44.600
…nominal trajectory.

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:47.390
Second-stage propulsion is nominal.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:50.360
First-stage advance
towards Spaceport Oita.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:58.200
Yes! I've finally hacked
the reflex function.

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:04.160
I guess I have to remove
the C limiter next.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:10.170
Well, then. Hack Twelve's database
like always and continue learning.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:14.670
Hurry up and start Lunatic.
Then go past Seven.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:18.010
Never mind that, Touya.
You're going to be late for PT.

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:20.890
Damn. I forgot.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:24.890
Second-stage shutdown.
Launch escape system is disarmed.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:28.730
Entering inertial guidance.

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:32.520
You may now use the Internet.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:36.030
You may unfasten your seat belts.
Enjoy zero gravity.

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:37.860
We finally made it!

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:41.070
Three, two--

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.200
It's Mina, everybody!

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:46.450
Okay, sorry for the delay, everyone.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:50.330
SkyTuber Mina, here.
Resuming live commentary.

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:52.630
The polar lights are amazing.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:56.380
I'm going to try out zero gravity
right away.

00:02:57.670 --> 00:03:00.760
Bathroom! Where is the bathroom?

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:03.470
I'm gonna go in this.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.310
Just go in that, please.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.060
Oh, yeah, that's right.

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:12.310
The boy is doing his business in
his diapers and getting too close to me.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.940
Space is hell. I'm going to puke.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:18.070
I don't think you should talk
to your little brother like that.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.150
I see the Anshin.

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:25.370
Have a look on the right.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:29.120
There's the Anshin commercial station,
the pride of Japan.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.460
It's tiny!

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:32.620
You can't even see it.

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:38.000
And now a word from Twelve,
the station's host AI.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:41.510
Welcome to Space Hotel Anshin of Japan.

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:45.140
It seems this station
is called the Anshin.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:46.220
LAME

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:49.890
I wonder who gave it
such an exceedingly stupid name.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:51.890
It's ONIQLO!

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:55.230
Oh, no. Nasa will kill me if I'm late.

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:58.610
Also, Touya, sorry to bring it up again.

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:00.530
Come here, Dakky.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:03.490
What do you want, Chief?

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:06.820
Will you get out of my room now?

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:10.540
Don't you actually have a room
on the Earth floor below?

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:14.250
Yes, okay. See you next month.

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:17.290
That's what you said last month.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:25.260
Earth is no environment
for humans to live in.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:29.390
Humans should live extraterrestrially.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:48.370
EPISODE 1:
EXTRATERRESTRIAL EMISSARIES

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:50.410
I've finally seen the real thing.

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:53.250
Yanegawara tiles!

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:55.330
This space station has yanegawara tiles.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:56.420
LANTERN

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:58.420
That's Japan-made for you.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:00.920
No way! Something even better! A crab!

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.010
SERIOUSLY?

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:05.930
The space station has a crab on it.
Perfect for a post!

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:08.800
How awful! Mars and the moon are skewered.

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:10.760
-OUCH
-MINA IS MEAN

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:13.140
What unbelievable taste.

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:15.940
What could it possibly be like inside?

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.730
Igniting thruster for altitude adjustment.

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:18.810
CURRENT FOLLOWER COUNT

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:21.320
There will be some turbulence.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:24.570
-Please return to your seat.
-Mina, get in your seat.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:27.320
-Please fasten your seat belt.
-Mina!

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:31.830
Our shuttle will be igniting a thruster
for altitude adjustment shortly.

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:34.250
This is why I don't like space.

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:39.330
-Can I eat these?
-Sure.

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:44.670
Please don't make a mess with the nuts.

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:48.760
Excuse me.

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:51.640
I'm Taiyou Tsukuba.

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:54.430
Did you guys come here
for the Deegle promotion too?

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:58.850
Yes. I'm Hiroshi Tanegashima.
Everybody calls me Hakase.

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:01.310
I'm from Saitama, on Earth.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.190
That's my older sister, Mina Misasa.

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:05.740
Our parents are divorced,
so we have different last names.

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:07.490
She's a LoserTuber.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:10.620
Do losers have
hundreds of thousands of followers?

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:12.330
Nice to meet you. Want me to follow you?

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:13.410
MINA MISASA
FOLLOWERS: 100,432

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:14.410
No.

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:15.700
TAIYOU TSUKUBA - FOLLOWERS: 3
HIROSHI TANEGASHIMA - FOLLOWERS: 81

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:17.540
I only use it
to stay in touch with people.

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:21.170
Hundreds of thousands is nothing
compared to Touya.

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:22.420
TOUYA SAGAMI:
14 YEARS OLD, BORN ON THE MOON

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.170
-Who?
-The other participant.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:26.300
The other?

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:28.510
Sagami! Touya Sagami.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:31.890
He's famous. He was the last kid
born extraterrestrially.

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:33.470
Never heard of him.

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:42.110
-He has 100 million followers.
-Seriously? Well, he must be just lovely.

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:43.560
TOUYA SAGAMI
FOLLOWERS: 100,010

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:45.860
Stay in your cradle, Earther!

00:06:56.330 --> 00:07:01.870
Anshin Japan Ex-terra 607
cleared for capture-point zero approach.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:04.750
Go for auto-capture sequence…

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:09.630
Originally, wasn't ICS
supposed to have been destroyed in 2017?

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:12.840
Japan Ex-terra 607,
you are berthing at Port 03.

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:23.860
KONOHA B. NANASE - FOLLOWERS: 7

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:28.820
CHECK-UP TIME

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:30.530
Gotta pick up the medicine.

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:42.920
I'm stuck with extra gravity
just because the Earthers have come.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:48.630
Just my imagination?

00:07:56.260 --> 00:08:00.060
What a pain.
Nobody actually benefits from gravity.

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:02.560
Dakky, wait here.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:17.780
What's this?

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:22.040
-What is it?
-There's something strange over there.

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:24.500
Something strange? Like a UFO?

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:28.250
Just a shooting star.

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:29.420
A shooting star?

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:35.300
Error code 4423 has been detected.

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:38.800
Seems like it's an AI malfunction.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:43.020
What does that mean?

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:44.480
I don't really know.

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:45.810
Checking the system.

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:49.650
I sense an unidentified projectile
not on the navigation list.

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:53.190
What altitude?

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:55.280
It was launched from a low orbit.

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:57.070
Its current altitude is 800 kilometers.

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:58.950
It's turning away.

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:00.580
No risk of collision.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:03.000
Uchinoura, where did the launch originate?

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:04.210
I don't know.

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:06.460
What a pain.

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:08.830
Nobeyama, report it to UN2.

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:10.840
Already reported.

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:12.960
-What--
-What's the matter?

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:15.050
I've found the origin of launch.

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:17.720
-It seems it was UN2.
-What?

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:21.350
The projectile is hiding
on the other side of Earth.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:26.350
What do I do when UN2
is breaking navigation rules?

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:35.860
TARGET: 3000 M

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:37.610
Wait a minute, Touya.

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:40.950
Didn't I tell you no hacking the facility?

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:42.490
Do your PT properly.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:49.420
How is this therapy?

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:52.460
I was just born on the moon.
It's not like I'm sick.

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:54.510
Look, just keep doing it.

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:08.140
Dakky, you okay?

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:12.860
Okay, breathe in.

00:10:13.690 --> 00:10:15.360
Breathe out.

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:17.860
Twelve, what do you think?

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:19.860
One moment.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:23.490
-Touya's heartbeat is increasing.
-Ouch!

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:27.040
Hey, don't be a perv. Turn around.

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:31.080
Don't hit my head.
What if my implant broke?

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:34.380
How's Konoha doing?

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:35.460
PASSWORD

00:10:35.550 --> 00:10:37.880
That's personal information,
so I won't tell you.

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:41.930
Konoha's implant
isn't dissolving well either, is it?

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:43.850
Are you still talking?

00:10:43.930 --> 00:10:47.520
That's just an urban legend that kids
with eighth-grade syndrome came up with.

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:49.480
Don't make a fool of me.

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:52.770
All right. I'm going to give you
the usual gravity-sickness medicine.

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:53.860
Wait over there.

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:55.730
PHARMACY AUTO-DISPENSER
FROM NASA WITH LOVE

00:10:56.900 --> 00:11:00.110
I'm in the eighth grade, so I'm supposed
to have eighth-grade syndrome.

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:01.200
GRAVITY

00:11:03.070 --> 00:11:05.830
-Twelve.
-Yes, what is it?

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:10.830
Touya's implant was designed by Seven,
the smartest AI ever.

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:12.080
INTRODUCTION TO SEVEN POEM

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:17.460
Yes. At the time, its product development
was done by Seven Technology,

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:20.720
but they went bankrupt
in the so-called Lunatic Seven incident.

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:23.550
Yeah, I know.

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:27.470
But why did Seven make
such a mistake in design?

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:32.560
I do not even have a tenth of Seven's
intelligence, so I do not know.

00:11:36.610 --> 00:11:38.030
UNCLE

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:41.950
-Yeah?
-You at the gym right now?

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:43.490
Yeah.

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:45.780
Did you go running
like you're supposed to?

00:11:45.870 --> 00:11:48.700
If you don't build up your stamina,
you can't go down to Earth.

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:51.210
I'm not going to Earth.

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:52.290
GRAVITY

00:11:52.370 --> 00:11:54.130
I wanna be at your place.

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:56.210
We talked about this the other day.

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:59.590
Off-Earthers can't adopt any kids.

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:00.880
I'm not a kid.

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:02.130
NOW YOUR FAMILY CAN HAVE SPACE!

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:03.590
I know everything.

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:04.680
LET'S GO TO SPACE

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:06.600
I know what they say on Earther Internet.

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:08.430
What are you talking about?

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:13.310
That kids born in space should just die
with their faulty implants.

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:15.600
Don't take that stuff seriously.

00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:22.070
Does God exist in space too?

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:23.820
God?

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:27.370
If there is a god out in space,

00:12:27.950 --> 00:12:31.000
he's a useless slacker.

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:35.040
Touya, God won't do anything for you.

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:39.250
The only things that will save you
are your own efforts

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:41.920
and the science and technology
created by people.

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:46.340
I wish a meteorite would fall
and destroy Earth.

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:48.300
CALL ENDED

00:12:48.390 --> 00:12:49.680
He hung up?

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:51.270
Was that Touya?

00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:56.060
Yeah. An already complicated kid
has reached a complicated age.

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:59.690
By the way, Mayor, we have a complaint
coming in about the space bungee.

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:01.730
It seems the bungee has stopped.

00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:06.820
Also, UN2 wants us to scrap
the unauthorized ICS antenna right away.

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:08.240
Yeah, got it.

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:11.830
About that projectile from before,
did UN2 respond?

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:14.460
No reply.

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:18.960
Geez. What do we have an organization
like the United Nations for?

00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:21.710
Now Nasa's complaining.

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:23.710
Is it her again?

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:26.470
Yes, yes. Complaints Officer.

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:28.470
Yes, this is Nasa.

00:13:29.090 --> 00:13:31.560
I told you I can't handle kids.

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:34.480
Why did you foist another one on me?

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:36.560
MARS GRAVITY FLOOR

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:48.660
Konoha, weren't you going to be
at the Earthers' dinner?

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:51.450
Yeah, but Nasa stopped me.

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:54.160
I see. Come on, Dakky.

00:13:58.210 --> 00:14:00.210
How's your implant?

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:02.250
I don't know.

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:05.260
I've been playing around with mine.

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:08.930
I've figured out
where most of its bugs are.

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:10.720
I'm going to try and fix them.

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:14.850
I think the reflection port
is what is encrypted.

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:17.140
-Do you know what that is?
-No.

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:20.810
If it goes well with mine,
I'll fix yours too.

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:23.480
You'll get in trouble with Nasa again.

00:14:24.110 --> 00:14:25.730
As if I care.

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:37.080
But aren't you happy
you're working off-Earth like you wanted?

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:39.540
I mean, your name is Nasa Houston.

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:42.080
Are you going to bring that up again?

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:47.090
In that case, let me tell you
I am both a nurse and a caregiver.

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:50.220
Yet I'm only getting paid
for one of those jobs.

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:52.340
This is space-staff exploitation.

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:54.760
I'm going to tell the personnel AI.

00:14:54.850 --> 00:14:57.770
Yeah, but the personnel AI
is the one that made the decision.

00:14:57.850 --> 00:14:59.520
Oh, hang on a second.

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:02.770
-What is it?
-The verdict's come in on the projectile.

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:05.230
This can't be.

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:08.490
Yes, this is a military-- What?

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:17.040
I wonder if I'll soon be cursed and die.

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:20.750
What was that?

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:27.000
-Now what?
-Maybe a CME?

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:29.050
A communications error.

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:33.260
This isn't just a communications error.

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:34.390
What?

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:35.890
OUT OF RANGE

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:38.560
Please do not unfasten
your seat belts yet--

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:40.270
BLOCKED BY UNKNOWN ERROR

00:15:42.270 --> 00:15:44.310
The Internet! There's no Internet!

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:46.150
What's happening to the system?

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:49.320
-Twelve.
-Twelve is down. Rebooting.

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:51.400
Twelve is down?

00:15:51.490 --> 00:15:55.120
-I can't use any of the control systems.
-What about the debris shield?

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:58.580
The debris shield is also down.
We're completely exposed to debris.

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:00.870
How long will it take to reboot Twelve?

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:03.580
Twelve isn't functioning, so I don't know.

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:06.840
We'll manually reboot the shields only.

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:09.340
What? You can do that?

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:13.260
I don't know, but there was a section
on it in the printed manual.

00:16:13.930 --> 00:16:15.800
Konoha, are you okay?

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:19.600
I've been hearing a strange sound.

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:21.680
No worries, Konoha.

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:25.900
According to the Seven Poem,
we won't die right now.

00:16:27.270 --> 00:16:30.150
All right. I've rebooted the shield only.

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:37.160
Is this that thing that goes off one time
as a test when you reboot?

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:39.870
Debris detected. This is the real thing.

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:42.080
Initiate interception sequence!

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:44.160
What do we do about the target data?

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:46.750
Can we use the off-line calculator?

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:48.920
Calculate with your own Smart.

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:55.180
I can't do my live feed
without the Internet.

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:58.140
What's this, a terrorist attack?

00:16:58.220 --> 00:17:00.310
What? Is terrorism still a thing nowadays?

00:17:00.390 --> 00:17:02.310
It happened last year too.

00:17:02.390 --> 00:17:05.560
They tried to target the space elevator
that was under construction.

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:06.850
I know about that.

00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:10.020
John Doe, right?
The mysterious superhacker group.

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:12.820
Smells like a scoop.

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:15.320
Mina here, everyone!

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:16.410
RECORDING: OFF-LINE

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:18.450
I'm not sure about this,
but I'll just make the video.

00:17:19.030 --> 00:17:21.200
Twelve has partially rebooted.

00:17:22.660 --> 00:17:25.330
Damn it! Nothing makes sense!

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:28.830
It sounds like something
really interesting is happening! No fair!

00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:32.210
Normally, no celestial objects
are in this kind of orbit.

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:33.880
Is it artificial?

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:35.880
Maybe an Apollo stage three?

00:17:35.970 --> 00:17:37.970
We won't know unless Twelve is working.

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:41.640
-We should put our helmets on.
-Okay.

00:17:43.970 --> 00:17:46.060
Mina, put yours on too.

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:48.560
I'm inside the shuttle now.

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:50.900
If we hit something,
we could die in an instant.

00:17:50.980 --> 00:17:52.650
Mina's in big trouble.

00:17:52.730 --> 00:17:54.820
-I wonder if this is debris.
-De-what?

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:56.820
Debris. Space junk.

00:17:56.900 --> 00:17:59.240
If it was debris,
we would know its position.

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:02.280
So it must be a small celestial body.
It's dangerous.

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:04.750
It must be a small celestial body.
It's dangerous.

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:05.830
Be original!

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:07.460
No shield yet?

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:10.460
Shield-drone reboot complete.

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:13.340
-What about the estimated course?
-Done.

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:15.760
Confirming specification input.

00:18:15.840 --> 00:18:16.840
Fire!

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:20.340
Please let the calculations be right.

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:27.730
If it hits us and we die, I wonder
if I'll get over 100 million followers.

00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:33.440
Confirming shield-deployment signal.

00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:36.610
Targeted debris will collide
with the shields in 21 seconds.

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:42.320
Well, will we actually be turned into
a fine dust and die?

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:44.870
If you are interested,
subscribe to my channel.

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:46.830
Impact in five seconds.

00:18:46.910 --> 00:18:48.460
Three, two--

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:52.250
It's too far away. I can't see anything.

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:55.960
Trajectory altered by 0.32 degrees.

00:18:56.050 --> 00:18:57.510
Collision evaded!

00:18:59.590 --> 00:19:01.260
They said the collision was evaded.

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:03.760
Wow!

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:07.180
The Internet's on.

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:10.270
Hey, I've safely survived.

00:19:10.350 --> 00:19:12.650
More to come after we deboard.

00:19:12.730 --> 00:19:15.190
SkyTuber Mina signing off.

00:19:15.270 --> 00:19:17.440
Mina, everybody!

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:21.610
This means
something has hacked the system.

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:24.620
Please remain seated.

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:27.200
Please do not unfasten your seat belt.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:29.290
Warning lifted.

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:31.580
Twelve has rebooted.

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:37.170
I am Deegle's advanced general purpose AI,
Twelve.

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:40.130
-With the prosperity and development--
-Shut up.

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:41.300
Shutting up.

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:44.970
Twelve, analyze the components
of the celestial body.

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:47.680
Most of it is ice.

00:19:47.760 --> 00:19:48.810
Ice?

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:50.890
This is part of a comet.

00:19:50.980 --> 00:19:52.310
A comet?

00:19:52.390 --> 00:19:54.480
What's a comet doing in such a low orbit?

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:58.190
I don't know, but more importantly,
what about the penetrating orbit?

00:19:58.280 --> 00:19:59.860
What about the penetrating orbit?

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:02.200
The source
of the communications malfunction earlier

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:03.820
intersects with the orbit.

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:07.490
I can't get in the room.

00:20:10.660 --> 00:20:12.080
It's cold!

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:14.960
What is UN2 saying?

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:18.250
Nothing yet.
The communications system is unstable.

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:21.260
Don't the AIs fully automate
the communications system?

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:25.840
Yes, but it looks like AI is down
in different areas.

00:20:25.930 --> 00:20:29.510
See? This is why you can't trust AI.

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:32.390
This ability
wasn't built into its learning.

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:35.060
It looks like it has entered
the learning process.

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:37.190
So what should we do?

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:39.110
Nothing at this point.

00:20:39.190 --> 00:20:41.900
Oh, yeah, what should we do
about the welcome party?

00:20:41.990 --> 00:20:44.400
We have that as well.

00:20:45.070 --> 00:20:47.820
We can't even leave that to the AIs.

00:20:52.410 --> 00:20:55.790
You can collect your luggage
after quarantine.

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:59.290
-We made it. Look!
-Wow.

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:04.800
There really is an Earth.

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:07.800
Of course there is.

00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:12.060
Yeah,
but I've only ever seen it on a screen.

00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:16.270
I didn't think it could be real
or that it would be so lovely.

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:20.070
What's that sound?

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:23.490
What is this?

00:21:24.780 --> 00:21:26.070
Greetings.

00:21:26.150 --> 00:21:29.490
I am Anshin-kun, the station fairy.

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:33.120
Well, everyone, welcome to the Anshin.

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:36.620
I am Sagami, the mayor. How do you do?

00:21:37.500 --> 00:21:38.960
Hello.

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:43.960
Congratulations for winning the Deegle's
Youth Space Experience promotion.

00:21:44.050 --> 00:21:46.840
As a space hotel,
it is the fourth ever built in the world,

00:21:46.930 --> 00:21:52.600
but this is the first space hotel
equipped with guest facilities for minors.

00:21:52.680 --> 00:21:54.350
Relax and enjoy.

00:21:54.930 --> 00:21:55.930
We will.

00:21:56.020 --> 00:21:57.850
Well then, I'll see you at dinner.

00:22:05.740 --> 00:22:08.740
What? Aren't you going to dinner, Chief?

00:22:08.820 --> 00:22:10.950
My back hurts.

00:22:11.030 --> 00:22:13.990
I'm going to the A Cylinder spa.

00:22:14.830 --> 00:22:18.080
The chief's skipping too? Everybody is.

00:22:19.370 --> 00:22:20.750
All right.

00:22:20.830 --> 00:22:23.170
Next, if I do Smart pairing…

00:22:23.920 --> 00:22:26.840
What? What--

00:22:28.050 --> 00:22:32.930
Oh, I see. If I straighten my legs
and focus my center of gravity…

00:22:33.010 --> 00:22:35.020
Okay.

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:38.850
Wow.

00:22:42.440 --> 00:22:46.150
Wow. This floor is made out of fabric.

00:22:47.280 --> 00:22:49.240
Wow.

00:22:57.500 --> 00:22:59.460
I'm getting the hang of it.

00:22:59.540 --> 00:23:01.830
-Where is Mina?
-Dunno.

00:23:02.460 --> 00:23:08.220
Sorry to keep you… waiting.

00:23:10.970 --> 00:23:13.010
Mina, everybody!

00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:19.020
I've won the Anshin Youth
Space Vacation Tour promotion.

00:23:19.520 --> 00:23:22.730
Which just means you get diapers,
eat, sleep, then go home.

00:23:23.610 --> 00:23:25.230
And here we have--

00:23:26.070 --> 00:23:27.320
Where is this?

00:23:27.820 --> 00:23:29.650
This is the elevator hall.

00:23:29.740 --> 00:23:32.610
I'm Nasa. I'm an attendant.

00:23:33.700 --> 00:23:34.950
Wow.

00:23:35.030 --> 00:23:36.990
Now we will head to dinner.

00:23:37.490 --> 00:23:38.500
-Okay.
-Okay.

00:23:40.040 --> 00:23:41.500
-What?
-What?

00:23:41.580 --> 00:23:45.500
-The Anshin is the first facility…
-This is Anshin Hills.

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:49.130
It says "Hills,"
but I'm not sure which way is up.

00:23:49.800 --> 00:23:53.260
-Wait. What is that?
-A water tank.

00:23:53.840 --> 00:23:55.180
Crabs!

00:23:55.260 --> 00:23:57.970
We also breed crabs here.

00:23:58.470 --> 00:24:00.480
You can eat your space food there.

00:24:00.560 --> 00:24:01.890
SAFETY VENDING MACHINE

00:24:01.980 --> 00:24:03.400
-Okay.
-Okay.

00:24:03.480 --> 00:24:04.650
-Space food!
-Space food!

00:24:04.730 --> 00:24:08.360
-The latest space food.
-What is this? It looks like ice cream.

00:24:08.940 --> 00:24:10.900
These are sweets!

00:24:10.990 --> 00:24:12.900
This alone makes a meal.

00:24:12.990 --> 00:24:14.780
Space is awesome!

00:24:14.870 --> 00:24:16.620
Steak! There's ramen too.

00:24:16.700 --> 00:24:18.540
I'll try the steak.

00:24:21.250 --> 00:24:24.670
It tastes… like chicken.

00:24:24.750 --> 00:24:26.790
I wonder what space meat is.

00:24:26.880 --> 00:24:28.210
Who knows?

00:24:28.300 --> 00:24:29.840
You're eating it right up regardless.

00:24:30.590 --> 00:24:31.590
Who's that?

00:24:31.670 --> 00:24:34.430
Could it be… Touya?

00:24:36.720 --> 00:24:40.520
Yes. This is Touya,
famous on a cosmic scale.

00:24:40.600 --> 00:24:42.060
Hey, say hello.

00:24:44.390 --> 00:24:49.440
Well,
this Youth Space Invitation promotion

00:24:49.520 --> 00:24:53.650
shows how Deegle offers you every service
from prenatal care to space burial--

00:24:53.740 --> 00:24:56.200
-IS THIS TOUYA?
-SOMEONE FAMOUS

00:24:56.280 --> 00:24:58.740
That is Touya,
famous across the cosmos.

00:24:59.330 --> 00:25:02.750
I've been a fan for so long.
Now I've seen him in person.

00:25:03.330 --> 00:25:05.870
Well, I--

00:25:05.960 --> 00:25:08.710
as the last kid born on the moon--

00:25:08.790 --> 00:25:13.670
I receive free humanitarian aid
from Deegle.

00:25:14.470 --> 00:25:19.470
Deegle's comprehensive services,
benefiting all of society,

00:25:19.550 --> 00:25:22.390
are what I am so very thankful for.

00:25:22.470 --> 00:25:23.600
The end.

00:25:27.980 --> 00:25:30.020
Watch your attitude, Touya.

00:25:30.110 --> 00:25:33.320
Have Konoha speak next time.
Don't always call on me to do this.

00:25:39.450 --> 00:25:41.280
-SPACE JUICE
-SEEMS THEY DRINK COMET WATER

00:25:41.370 --> 00:25:44.830
Nice to meet you. You--
You're Touya, right?

00:25:45.790 --> 00:25:48.080
Yeah, I guess.

00:25:48.170 --> 00:25:50.340
Wow! You know what?

00:25:50.420 --> 00:25:52.800
I'm a follower of yours.

00:25:52.880 --> 00:25:54.340
Wow, I said it.

00:25:59.430 --> 00:26:01.640
Thank you for following.

00:26:01.720 --> 00:26:03.270
I'm a huge fan!

00:26:03.350 --> 00:26:06.230
I've read everything. Even the conspiracy
theories on your secret account.

00:26:06.310 --> 00:26:08.190
Everything you wrote is true.

00:26:08.770 --> 00:26:14.940
By limiting AI cognition,
UN2 is trapping humanity in a cradle.

00:26:15.030 --> 00:26:19.660
Is it true the way to destroy the cradle
is written down in the Seven Poem?

00:26:19.740 --> 00:26:22.530
And then,
just like on your secret account,

00:26:22.620 --> 00:26:26.000
I also believe that the Seven implants
are faulty products-- Ouch.

00:26:26.080 --> 00:26:28.080
Ouch!

00:26:30.330 --> 00:26:32.590
What are you doing to my little brother?

00:26:32.670 --> 00:26:34.800
It's just an ultrasonic head flick.

00:26:34.880 --> 00:26:36.210
It's safe and secure.

00:26:36.800 --> 00:26:38.090
I'm fine.

00:26:38.170 --> 00:26:41.090
Earthers should stay in their cradle.

00:26:41.180 --> 00:26:44.350
Don't act so arrogant just because
you have 100 million followers!

00:26:44.430 --> 00:26:49.600
Bright, the unauthorized access detected
in the shuttle was definitely that drone.

00:26:49.690 --> 00:26:53.320
Yes, I've discovered
an artificial intelligence law violation.

00:26:53.400 --> 00:26:56.570
The error goes all the way
to a B limiter in the lower level.

00:26:56.650 --> 00:26:58.740
Criminal arrest of the offender
is possible.

00:26:58.820 --> 00:27:01.990
-I need to a put a collar on them then.
-Aye. Copy.

00:27:02.070 --> 00:27:04.910
We should drop a meteorite
or a comet on the Earth

00:27:04.990 --> 00:27:07.910
and reduce the population by one-third
while we have the chance.

00:27:08.000 --> 00:27:10.620
It's for your own good, you Earthers.

00:27:11.210 --> 00:27:13.210
You're really screwed up.

00:27:13.290 --> 00:27:17.130
Otherwise, humans will
overpopulate themselves into extinction.

00:27:17.210 --> 00:27:21.220
Hey, Touya! You'll breach your
contract if you don't stay until the end.

00:27:21.890 --> 00:27:23.850
What unfortunate news.

00:27:23.930 --> 00:27:27.930
Our beloved Touya is a cosmic loser.

00:27:28.020 --> 00:27:32.190
That kid is sick. The name of his disease
is likely eighth-grade syndrome.

00:27:32.770 --> 00:27:34.690
Touya is awesome!

00:27:34.770 --> 00:27:38.740
Seriously. Just like my older brother was
when he was a kid.

00:27:38.820 --> 00:27:42.820
Mayor, this is an emergency. Please come
to the control room immediately.

00:27:42.910 --> 00:27:45.370
That drone doesn't connect
to the Internet?

00:27:45.450 --> 00:27:46.870
Then how?

00:27:46.950 --> 00:27:49.250
It is probably using a peer comm.

00:27:49.330 --> 00:27:51.000
A proximity connection?

00:27:51.080 --> 00:27:53.170
I attack with a peer comm too.

00:27:53.750 --> 00:27:57.170
But peer comms
have to be within five meters.

00:27:59.550 --> 00:28:01.930
Okay, I'll create a diversion.

00:28:02.010 --> 00:28:04.050
-Make your approach in that opening.
-Copy.

00:28:07.350 --> 00:28:10.850
-You're Touya Sagami, right?
-What do you want?

00:28:10.930 --> 00:28:14.810
Your drone's cognitive limiter is off,
isn't it?

00:28:14.900 --> 00:28:17.320
Bright, force access to that drone.

00:28:19.320 --> 00:28:20.400
Copy.

00:28:21.150 --> 00:28:22.860
What are you doing?

00:28:23.860 --> 00:28:26.700
-Stop that kid's function!
-Aye. Copy.

00:28:27.700 --> 00:28:28.790
A peer comm?

00:28:28.870 --> 00:28:29.950
Bright.

00:28:31.290 --> 00:28:32.660
Don't let him get away.

00:28:37.040 --> 00:28:37.960
Wha--

00:28:38.040 --> 00:28:41.170
Setting up a peer comm for me? Dark!

00:28:43.220 --> 00:28:44.590
Bright, let go!

00:28:46.680 --> 00:28:49.470
Damn it. Closing the distance
in the opening-- Wha--

00:28:49.560 --> 00:28:52.430
Take cover!
Where is the attack coming from?

00:28:56.900 --> 00:28:58.060
Ouch!

00:28:58.150 --> 00:28:59.980
Through peer comms in the wall?

00:29:00.610 --> 00:29:04.950
You're 13.8 billion years behind me
in a peer comm match.

00:29:05.030 --> 00:29:08.160
Bright,
grant permission for use of the UN2 code.

00:29:08.240 --> 00:29:10.870
Overwrite nearby peer comm devices
with the UN2 code.

00:29:11.910 --> 00:29:12.910
Copy.

00:29:14.910 --> 00:29:17.290
Dark, overwrite with enhanced coding.

00:29:22.880 --> 00:29:25.380
I knew it.
That's an illegal drone, isn't it?

00:29:26.010 --> 00:29:27.840
Who the hell are you?

00:29:28.430 --> 00:29:32.060
I am a White Hat Hacker
with UN2.1 authorization--

00:29:32.140 --> 00:29:33.430
Taiyou Tsukuba.

00:29:33.520 --> 00:29:37.730
And I am the UN2.1 official drone--
Bright.

00:29:39.150 --> 00:29:43.360
Your drone is like a dog without a collar,
in a manner of speaking.

00:29:43.440 --> 00:29:46.700
I'm the one who cracks down on that
and puts a collar on--

00:29:51.200 --> 00:29:53.120
Wait!

00:29:53.200 --> 00:29:55.040
Wait. What you are guys doing?

00:29:58.040 --> 00:29:59.500
Touya!

00:29:59.580 --> 00:30:03.000
Honestly, how many times
have I told you not to go down there?

00:30:03.090 --> 00:30:04.210
Hang on!

00:30:05.670 --> 00:30:07.090
Oh, no.

00:30:09.300 --> 00:30:14.060
It's terrible. Two boys have jumped down
and committed suicide.

00:30:14.140 --> 00:30:15.810
I'll follow them with the camera.

00:30:16.560 --> 00:30:20.650
It's highly possible the communication
malfunction was from an EMP.

00:30:20.730 --> 00:30:22.570
An EMP? That can't be.

00:30:22.650 --> 00:30:25.440
These are electromagnetic waves
from a nuclear explosion.

00:30:25.530 --> 00:30:27.030
A nuclear explosion?

00:30:27.110 --> 00:30:28.570
That's not all.

00:30:28.660 --> 00:30:32.740
The nuclear attack targeted
another projectile to intercept it.

00:30:32.830 --> 00:30:35.290
Another projectile? What on earth?

00:30:35.370 --> 00:30:36.700
What are you guys doing?

00:30:36.790 --> 00:30:39.460
We'll also follow them down
in the elevator.

00:30:39.540 --> 00:30:41.210
Hurry! Down below!

00:30:42.290 --> 00:30:45.210
Don't follow me!
It's impossible for Earthers!

00:30:45.300 --> 00:30:47.760
Don't underestimate me. Bright!

00:30:50.010 --> 00:30:51.010
Oops!

00:30:51.090 --> 00:30:54.510
What the hell? Dakky, take him down.

00:30:56.810 --> 00:30:59.140
Coriolis adjustment in progress. Cori--

00:31:04.150 --> 00:31:06.400
Down just like that, Bright!

00:31:08.780 --> 00:31:12.280
That's why I said it was impossible
for Earthers. Just turn back!

00:31:12.870 --> 00:31:14.410
I'm not turning back.

00:31:14.490 --> 00:31:15.990
-Do it, Bright!
-Aye. Copy.

00:31:24.880 --> 00:31:26.670
I'm getting a great shot!

00:31:26.750 --> 00:31:30.630
Oh, no.
It'll be my fault if he gets injured.

00:31:30.720 --> 00:31:32.930
Yes! My followers have doubled.

00:31:33.010 --> 00:31:35.930
I want to do that too. Can I?

00:31:36.010 --> 00:31:37.850
This is why I can't handle kids!

00:31:40.180 --> 00:31:42.810
Oh, no. My shoes ran out of gas.

00:31:44.310 --> 00:31:47.230
This is where you get off.
It's dangerous any lower.

00:31:49.690 --> 00:31:50.900
Oh, no!

00:31:51.780 --> 00:31:53.110
Grab on!

00:31:56.530 --> 00:31:57.740
Damn it!

00:31:59.160 --> 00:32:00.710
According to Twelve's analysis,

00:32:00.790 --> 00:32:03.290
the orbit where the communications
malfunction occurred

00:32:03.370 --> 00:32:06.880
was invaded by a small celestial body
captured by a water development company.

00:32:09.210 --> 00:32:11.010
Water? Comets?

00:32:11.090 --> 00:32:13.890
Yes. A commercial comet
that has been pulled to the earth

00:32:13.970 --> 00:32:16.800
in order to extract the water
and carbon to sell.

00:32:16.890 --> 00:32:17.890
DELICIOUS COMET WATER

00:32:19.220 --> 00:32:21.810
-The wall is getting closer.
-Push off the wall!

00:32:23.390 --> 00:32:25.810
We're going to jump before it catches up!

00:32:26.400 --> 00:32:28.070
It's gradually turning into a slope.

00:32:30.110 --> 00:32:31.740
Nice!

00:32:31.820 --> 00:32:33.110
Get off the chairs!

00:32:33.200 --> 00:32:36.570
But this path
isn't a commercial comet orbit.

00:32:36.660 --> 00:32:38.080
It's a collision course with the earth.

00:32:38.160 --> 00:32:41.200
Normally, it is supposed to be moored
in the moon's Lagrange.

00:32:41.290 --> 00:32:43.750
But something must have caused it
to go off track.

00:32:43.830 --> 00:32:45.880
Was it the target of the nuclear attack?

00:32:45.960 --> 00:32:48.290
Why didn't we get a notice
for something so important?

00:32:48.380 --> 00:32:51.380
On top of that, there's nothing
resembling comet fragments

00:32:51.460 --> 00:32:53.590
in the path calculated
from the nuclear explosion.

00:32:53.680 --> 00:32:54.930
What?

00:32:55.010 --> 00:32:59.720
In short, the nuclear attack failed,
and the comet could still be approaching.

00:32:59.810 --> 00:33:02.230
-The path is cut off!
-Damn it.

00:33:02.810 --> 00:33:04.600
Jump at the same time as I do!

00:33:05.900 --> 00:33:06.900
Now!

00:33:07.690 --> 00:33:09.320
Where is the comet now?

00:33:10.110 --> 00:33:14.650
Well, we don't have the data for that.
All of our orbit control systems are down.

00:33:14.740 --> 00:33:17.450
Have Twelve recalculate
with the data we have now!

00:33:18.030 --> 00:33:22.450
-The comet is low in Earth's orbit.
-What's the approximate altitude?

00:33:23.120 --> 00:33:25.960
400 to 300 kilometers!

00:33:27.420 --> 00:33:30.000
Wouldn't that be a direct hit
on the station?

00:33:30.090 --> 00:33:33.050
-What about the orbital plane?
-I don't know precisely.

00:33:33.130 --> 00:33:35.590
But it is very likely scattered
over a wide area,

00:33:35.680 --> 00:33:37.510
so there's a risk of collision.

00:33:37.590 --> 00:33:39.100
I've got visuals on the comet.

00:33:40.140 --> 00:33:43.730
The Earth's gravity is pulling it apart.
Seems it has broken into dozens of pieces.

00:33:43.810 --> 00:33:45.690
If we go up, we'll get hit.

00:33:45.770 --> 00:33:47.770
Drop the Anshin's altitude!

00:33:47.850 --> 00:33:49.400
Thruster deceleration!

00:33:49.480 --> 00:33:51.230
Issue a maximum-level alert!

00:33:51.820 --> 00:33:52.940
We're falling!

00:34:00.450 --> 00:34:01.580
What?

00:34:04.620 --> 00:34:07.250
-What?
-Hold on!

00:34:12.340 --> 00:34:14.260
KONOHA BAIKONUR NANASE

00:34:22.430 --> 00:34:24.140
We're going to collide!

00:34:34.730 --> 00:34:36.150
Dakky!

00:34:36.820 --> 00:34:38.780
Why are we accelerating?

00:34:39.360 --> 00:34:41.280
They're igniting the thrusters.

00:34:41.780 --> 00:34:43.330
Something happened.

00:34:43.950 --> 00:34:45.830
Current altitude is 320 kilometers.

00:34:45.910 --> 00:34:47.830
What is the Anshin's altitude limit?

00:34:47.910 --> 00:34:50.580
-180 kilometers.
-Drop us to 200!

00:34:50.670 --> 00:34:53.420
Use the plasma engine
and the moored shuttle!

00:34:57.050 --> 00:34:59.970
They're coming from below as well.
We can't evade them all!

00:35:00.550 --> 00:35:02.930
Everyone, this is Mayor Sagami.

00:35:03.010 --> 00:35:04.970
We will be colliding with an object.

00:35:05.060 --> 00:35:06.720
You all must hold on to something!

00:35:07.560 --> 00:35:09.980
-Evacuate to the shelters on all floors…
-A collision?

00:35:10.060 --> 00:35:11.730
…and ensure your own safety.

00:35:12.310 --> 00:35:15.690
Those in zero gravity,
please secure yourselves.

00:35:17.360 --> 00:35:19.150
The partition is closing.

00:35:19.990 --> 00:35:22.030
Something is coming this way.

00:35:22.120 --> 00:35:24.280
Hold on to me!

00:35:27.540 --> 00:35:30.670
Here comes the attack.

00:35:36.250 --> 00:35:37.670
It stopped.

00:35:39.260 --> 00:35:41.050
Secure yourself to your seat.

00:35:41.630 --> 00:35:42.800
What?

00:35:42.890 --> 00:35:44.300
Hold on!

00:35:47.970 --> 00:35:48.980
Here it comes!

00:37:20.270 --> 00:37:23.690
Subtitle translation by:
Noelle Marie Hollister
